invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20.c
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: chacha20.c's use_avx512 answers 0 whatever the session's ch_cfg.cpu
  says, so no session runs the AVX-512 kernel and CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA picks
  no ChaCha20. Every vector passes, because the AVX2 kernel and the SSE2
  path compute the same bytes; only the time is wrong. The script compiles
  chacha20.c for x86-64 and requires chacha20_xor_cpu to call the kernel.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA) != 0;
--- new
    (void)cpu;
    return 0;
